.TH LIBRDP-SERVER 1 "2026-07-19" "librdp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
librdp-server \- expose a native desktop through the librdp server runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librdp-server
.B --mode shadow
.B --allow-capture
.B --tls-cert
.I path
.B --tls-key
.I path
[
.I options
]
.PP
.B librdp-server
.B --mode managed
.B --managed-action
.I action
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librdp-server
shares a native display or window through the public librdp server API.
Capture, input, clipboard and client-drive providers require separate policy
grants. X11 builds also provide managed-session broker operations; macOS builds
provide shadow capture only.
.SH SHADOW OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --display " name"
Select the X display. The current
.B DISPLAY
value is used when omitted. X11 only.
.TP
.BI --source " selector"
Select the capture source. X11 accepts
.BR root ,
.B monitor:index
or
.BR window:id .
macOS accepts
.B display:index
or
.BR window:id .
.TP
.BI --bind " address"
Set the listener address. The default is loopback.
.TP
.BI --port " port"
Set the RDP listener port.
.TP
.BI --max-peers " count"
Limit concurrent peers.
.TP
.BI --max-fps " count"
Limit desktop capture and frame delivery to at most 60 frames per second.
.TP
.BI --max-frame-bytes " bytes"
Limit one captured BGRA frame to the configured byte count.
.TP
.BI --security " tls|nla|standard"
Select server security. TLS is the default.
.TP
.BI --tls-cert " path"
Load the TLS certificate from an absolute path.
.TP
.BI --tls-key " path"
Load the TLS private key from an absolute path.
.TP
.B --allow-standard-security
Permit explicitly selected Standard RDP Security.
.TP
.BI --user " name"
Set the account accepted by the configured authentication policy.
.TP
.BI --domain " name"
Set the accepted authentication domain.
.TP
.BI --password-env " name"
Read the authentication secret from the named environment variable.
.TP
.B --allow-capture
Grant access to the selected desktop source.
.TP
.B --allow-input
Grant remote keyboard and pointer injection.
.TP
.B --allow-clipboard
Grant bidirectional clipboard access.
.TP
.B --allow-drive
Grant access to client-announced drives.
.TP
.BI --drive-mount " path"
Select the isolated client-drive mount point.
.TP
.B --drive-read-only
Restrict client drives to read-only access.
.TP
.B --drive-read-write
Allow writes to client drives after explicit drive access has been granted.
.TP
.B --non-interactive
Do not request macOS privacy permissions or show local consent dialogs. Native
permissions must already be granted. macOS only.
.SH MANAGED OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --managed-action " start|attach|query|resize|detach|terminate"
Select the broker operation. X11 only.
.TP
.BI --broker " path"
Set the absolute broker Unix-socket path.
.TP
.BI --session-id " id"
Select an existing managed session.
.TP
.BI --token-env " name"
Read the reconnect token from the named environment variable.
.TP
.BI --width " pixels"
Set the requested managed desktop width.
.TP
.BI --height " pixels"
Set the requested managed desktop height.
.TP
.B --persistent
Request a desktop that may remain alive after detach.
.TP
.B --reconnect
Request a reconnect token.
.PP
The
.BR --user ,
.BR --domain ,
.BR --password-env ,
.BR --allow-capture ,
.BR --allow-input ,
.BR --allow-clipboard
and
.B --allow-drive
options also describe a managed start request. Broker policy can only remove
requested privileges. Managed options are available only in X11 builds.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --mode " shadow|managed"
Select the operating mode.
.TP
.B --help
Print command usage.
.SH SECURITY
Do not place passwords or reconnect tokens in command arguments. Use
.B --password-env
and
.B --token-env
with an environment visible only to the invoking account. Standard Security
is rejected unless explicitly enabled.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Revoke capture, input, clipboard and client-drive consent while keeping the
listener running. Existing input ownership and pending clipboard or drive
operations are released before their providers are disabled.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Stop the listener and release all peers and native providers.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp-session-broker (8),
.BR librdp-server (7),
.BR librdp (7)
